<SiteLayout title="Your project, explained | Avexel" description="A straightforward guide to working with Avexel: planning your website, collaborating on design, launching, and ongoing support.">
  <div class="wrap"><header class="page-intro"><a class="back-link" href="/">← Back to the studio</a><h1>Your project,<br />explained.</h1><p>A straightforward guide to working with our team, from the first conversation to life after launch.</p></header>
    <article class="guide">
      <h2>People first. Always.</h2><p>Avexel is a student-led design and development studio in Harbor Springs, Michigan. We work directly with businesses, nonprofits, and community organizations, and our projects help support Baywatch Robotics and STEM education.</p>
      <h2>What we can help with</h2><ul><li><strong>Design:</strong> a website that reflects your organization, with clear navigation and layouts for every screen.</li><li><strong>Development:</strong> custom websites, forms, booking tools, online stores, and integrations, scoped to your needs.</li><li><strong>Support:</strong> content changes, maintenance, and improvements as your organization grows.</li></ul>
      <h2>The first conversation</h2><p>You don’t need a finished brief. A rough idea is plenty. A few things are helpful to think about:</p><ul><li>Who is the website for, and what should visitors be able to do?</li><li>Do you have an existing website, brand assets, photos, or written content?</li><li>Are there specific features, deadlines, or budget considerations?</li><li>Who will provide feedback and look after the content?</li></ul>
      <h2>How the project moves forward</h2><ol><li><strong>Discovery & scope.</strong> We agree on the goals, pages, features, timeline, and price.</li><li><strong>Design & collaboration.</strong> You review the direction and provide feedback before the details are finalized.</li><li><strong>Development & testing.</strong> We build the site, share a preview, and check functionality across screens.</li><li><strong>Launch & handoff.</strong> We help configure the domain and hosting, publish the website, and explain how it works.</li></ol>
      <h2>Pricing without surprises</h2><p>Our <a href="/quote/">estimate builder</a> provides a starting point using your selected features and page count. Your final quote is based on the agreed scope. Domain registration, hosting, and third-party services are separate costs that we’ll discuss with you.</p><p>The website build is a one-time project cost. If you need ongoing updates or new features, we’ll agree on those separately.</p>
      <h2>Your website is yours</h2><p>You own your website’s code and content. You can choose where to host it and who maintains it. We can help with the technical setup and handoff.</p>
      <h2>After launch</h2><p>If something isn’t working, let us know. We’re also available for content updates, maintenance, and additional features. Support arrangements and any ongoing costs are discussed as part of your project.</p>
      <div class="glass"><h3>Have something in mind?</h3><p>Tell us a little about it. We’ll help work out the next step.</p><br /><a href="/#contact" class="button">Start a project <Icon name="arrowUpRight" /></a></div>
      <p>Prefer email? <a href="mailto:contact@avexel.co">contact@avexel.co</a><br />Or give us a call: <a href="tel:+12313738360">(231) 373-8360</a></p>
    </article>
  </div>
